---
import ProjectLayout from '../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro';
import Media from '../../components/Media.astro';
import MediaGrid from '../../components/MediaGrid.astro';
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Project Erwin"
  subtitle="An AI secretary that runs your day from voice, Obsidian, and a cloned command voice"
  tags={[
    { label: "Voice AI", href: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_synthesis" },
    { label: "Obsidian", href: "https://obsidian.md" },
    { label: "Piper TTS", href: "https://github.com/rhasspy/piper" },
    { label: "Telegram", href: "https://telegram.org" },
  ]}
>
  <section class="story-section">
    <h2>The Goal</h2>
    <p>
      Erwin is meant to be an AI secretary: it figures out your schedule, issues reminders and
      commands from what you tell it, and makes task logging low-friction. Logging work should
      not become its own productivity tax. The voice is Commander Erwin from Attack on Titan;
      the agent has access to whatever personal data you choose to give it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="story-section">
    <h2>How It Runs</h2>
    <p>
      Day-to-day context lives in an Obsidian vault (everything except high-sensitivity secrets
      like SSNs). The agent reads that vault to manage schedule and decide what to surface next,
      cutting the friction of "what should I do right now?"
    </p>
    <p>
      Voice was cloned and generated with ElevenLabs for dataset creation, then deployed
      locally with Piper TTS so replies can run without a cloud TTS bill. The local node
      talks over Telegram (text + voice notes) and handles deadline-aware reminders as a
      long-running service.
    </p>
    <p>
      The stack currently spans a Jarvis frontend node and a jarvis-backend / Erwin voice-weights
      pipeline; those repos are headed for a merge and rename under Project Erwin.
    </p>

    <!--
    <Media
      src="/assets/projects/erwin/telegram-thread.png"
      alt="Telegram conversation with Erwin"
      caption="Sample Telegram thread: schedule query + voice reply"
      aspect="9/16"
    />
    <Media
      src="/assets/projects/erwin/obsidian-context.png"
      alt="Obsidian vault context for Erwin"
      caption="Vault notes the agent uses for scheduling and priorities"
      aspect="16/9"
    />
    -->
  </section>

  <section class="story-section">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>
      Local Telegram + Piper voice path works. Voice-weight pipeline (clip harvest, ElevenLabs
      synthesis, fine-tune export) exists as a separate track. Next step is unifying the repos
      into one Erwin product surface.
    </p>
  </section>
</ProjectLayout>
